# {{ module_name }}

Poetry + pybind11 + CMake + vcpkg + GoogleTest + pytest.

## Reproducible setup and validation

From a fresh checkout:

```bash
python scripts/bootstrap.py
python scripts/validate.py --wheel
```

Requires Python 3.12+, Git and a platform C++17 toolchain (GCC/Clang on Linux; Visual Studio 2022 C++ tools and a Windows SDK on Windows). Linux also needs curl, zip, unzip and tar. Bootstrap installs pinned tools and the declared vcpkg baseline in `.dev-tools`. Validation configures, builds and runs CTest/pytest, then rebuilds a native wheel from the sdist and checks its installation in a clean environment.

The scripts supply tool paths automatically, including Ninja inside vcpkg compiler detection. Compiler tracking remains enabled. No shell activation or manual path setup is required.

